        "text": "Yes—given your interest in nature, photography and food, these would make great evening watches:\n\n- **My Octopus Teacher** (2020, 85 min): A filmmaker follows an octopus in a South African kelp forest. Intimate, visually beautiful and moving, with some tough wildlife moments.\n- **Finding Vivian Maier** (2013, 83 min): The discovery of a remarkable street photographer’s work opens up a mystery about her life. A good pick for your photography interests.\n- **Jiro Dreams of Sushi** (2011, 81 min): A portrait of a Tokyo sushi master, exploring craftsmanship, family and the pursuit of perfection.\n- **The Rescue** (2021, 107 min): The extraordinary rescue of a Thai youth football team from a flooded cave. Try this if you enjoyed the tension of *Free Solo*.\n- **Faces Places** (2017, 89 min): Filmmaker Agnès Varda and artist JR travel through rural France creating giant photographic portraits. Warm, playful and full of everyday stories.\n\n**My pick for tonight: *Faces Places*** if you want something uplifting, or *My Octopus Teacher* for an immersive nature watch. Streaming availability varies by country and service."
